{"parentUuid":"2c413f99-4050-4544-952b-e4eb31682949","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"73629415-2e82-45f7-8ec6-f5f9d1b1bd84","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FhumgJZinGWLCuY8r4F3LM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AOS-001 — Agentic Operating System for the SDLC\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** 10 (succeeds Phase 9 / pypes)\n4\t**Status:** DRAFT — pending OQ resolutions in [requirement.md §13](requirement.md#13-open-questions-must-be-resolved-before-phase-1-merges)\n5\t**Author:** Benny Studio team\n6\t**Last updated:** 2026-04-26\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## Purpose\n11\t\n12\tPhase 10 closes the loop between Benny's three capability surfaces (documents, code, tabular data) and turns Benny into a **deterministic, portable Agentic Operating System for the entire Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC)**. The driving artefact is the architectural brief *\"Architecting a Deterministic, Portable Agentic Operating System for the Software Development Life Cycle\"* (the **Brief**, attached to this folder as `source_brief.md` once committed).\n13\t\n14\tWhere Phase 9 (pypes) made tabular data first-class, Phase 10 makes the **agentic SDLC itself** a first-class citizen of the manifest schema:\n15\t\n16\t- Requirements → PRD → BDD acceptance criteria → manifest → execution → audit, all governed by one signed, replayable artefact.\n17\t- TOGAF ADM phases (A–D) become deterministic waves with hard quality gates between them.\n18\t- SOX 404 and BCBS 239 lineage become release-gated invariants, not afterthoughts.\n19\t\n20\tThis is **integration work**, not a rewrite. Every existing module — `SwarmManifest`, `swarm.py`, `manifest_runner.py`, `models.py`, `governance/`, `pypes/`, `persistence/checkpointer.py` — is extended, never replaced.\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t## Document set\n25\t\n26\t| Document | Role |\n27\t|----------|------|\n28\t| [README.md](README.md) | This index. Ground rules, vocabulary, do-not-do list. |\n29\t| [requirement.md](requirement.md) | **Normative.** Functional, non-functional, security, observability, and compliance requirements. Every claim is uniquely addressable. |\n30\t| [acceptance_matrix.md](acceptance_matrix.md) | Traceability matrix: every requirement ID → at least one test → status → evidence (SHA / CI run / file path). |\n31\t| [project_plan.md](project_plan.md) | The single tracking artefact: phase-by-phase plan, FMEA-style risk register, plan tracker checkboxes, KPI dashboard. Updated at the end of every session. |\n32\t| [open_questions.md](open_questions.md) | Pro/con analysis and recommendation for every OQ-* item before Phase 1 opens. Edit inline as decisions are taken. |\n33\t| `source_brief.md` (to be added) | Verbatim copy of the originating architectural brief, frozen for reference. |\n34\t\n35\t---\n36\t\n37\t## Glossary\n38\t\n39\t| Term | Definition |\n40\t|------|------------|\n41\t| **Agentic OS** | Benny's deterministic execution environment for AI agents. The \"OS\" boundary is the signed manifest + LangGraph state machine + governance middleware. |\n42\t| **SDLC manifest** | A `SwarmManifest` (schema_version ≥ 1.1) whose plan maps onto TOGAF ADM phases A–D and embeds BDD acceptance criteria as quality gates. |\n43\t| **Pass-by-reference (PBR)** | Tool outputs above `PBR_THRESHOLD_TOKENS` are stored in the artefact store and replaced in the LLM context with `${artifact://<sha>}`. |\n44\t| **Progressive disclosure** | Three-layer context loading (metadata → schema → full) governed by `benny/core/disclosure.py`. |\n45\t| **Quality gate** | A deterministic check (linter, type checker, BDD test, schema validator) that **must** return success before a wave advances. |\n46\t| **ADR** | Architecture Decision Record — auto-generated per SDLC phase under `data_out/adr/`. |\n47\t| **CDE** | Critical Data Element (BCBS 239 vocabulary). |\n48\t| **JSON-LD provenance** | An RDF-compatible JSON document recording prompt, model, inputs, outputs, hash chain, and ADR backlinks. |\n49\t| **Policy-as-Code** | Pre-execution intent check codified in `benny/governance/policy.py`. |\n50\t\n51\tVocabulary collisions between this folder and earlier requirement folders are resolved in this document's favour.\n52\t\n53\t---\n54\t\n55\t## Six-Sigma framing (why this folder is heavier than usual)\n56\t\n57\tPhase 10 touches financial-compliance code paths and the agent's ability to mutate the host filesystem. We adopt the same DPMO discipline that earlier phases used informally:\n58\t\n59\t1. **Define** — every requirement has a unique ID and a one-sentence success criterion ([requirement.md](requirement.md)).\n60\t2. **Measure** — every requirement has at least one test in [acceptance_matrix.md](acceptance_matrix.md) and a numeric or boolean target.\n61\t3. **Analyse** — failure modes are enumerated in the [risk register section of project_plan.md](project_plan.md#5-risk-register-fmea-style).\n62\t4. **Improve** — phases are ordered to retire the highest-RPN risks first.\n63\t5. **Control** — release gates `G-AOS-*` are appended to `docs/requirements/release_gates.yaml` and enforced by `tests/release/test_aos_release_gate.py`.\n64\t\n65\tA phase is **not done** until every acceptance row for that phase is `PASS` with a non-empty `Evidence` pointer **and** the relevant gate test is green on `master`.\n66\t\n67\t---\n68\t\n69\t## Do-not-do list (binding for any implementer agent or human)\n70\t\n71\t1. **Do not** call `litellm.completion` or any provider SDK directly. Always go through `benny.core.models.call_model()`. This is how `BENNY_OFFLINE=1`, lineage emission, AER capture, and cost telemetry fire.\n72\t2. **Do not** introduce new absolute paths to manifests, fixtures, configs, or tests. The SR-1 ratchet (≤ 408 violations) is a hard gate.\n73\t3. **Do not** bypass `sign_manifest()` / `verify_signature()`. Every manifest persisted under `$BENNY_HOME/workflows/` carries a HMAC-SHA256 signature.\n74\t4. **Do not** silently swallow `OfflineRefusal`. Cloud calls in offline mode must propagate to the user surface.\n75\t5. **Do not** widen `GOVERNANCE_WHITELIST`. New endpoints require `X-Benny-API-Key`.\n76\t6. **Do not** mutate run audit data from the sandbox layer (planner / agent-report / chat / sandbox runner). The deterministic core remains byte-replay-identical.\n77\t7. **Do not** check in `logs/`, `brain/`, or `$BENNY_HOME/`. They are git-ignored for good reason.\n78\t8. **Do not** flip `policy.auto_approve_writes` to `true`. It is reserved as a hard release-gate trip-wire (see [acceptance_matrix.md](acceptance_matrix.md) `GATE-AOS-POLICY-1`).\n79\t9. **Do not** bundle phases. One phase per PR. The plan tracker only ticks after the gate is green.\n80\t10. **Do not** answer an open question (OQ-*) by guessing. Pause and raise a HITL request.\n81\t\n82\t---\n83\t\n84\t## Quick links into the codebase (where new work lands)\n85\t\n86\t| Concern | Module path | Touch type |\n87\t|---------|-------------|------------|\n88\t| SDLC manifest fields | [benny/core/manifest.py](../../../benny/core/manifest.py) | additive |\n89\t| Pass-by-reference store | `benny/core/artifact_store.py` (new) | new |\n90\t| Progressive disclosure | `benny/core/disclosure.py` (new) | new |\n91\t| Mermaid / PlantUML emit | [benny/graph/wave_scheduler.py](../../../benny/graph/wave_scheduler.py), `benny/graph/diagrams.py` (new) | extend + new |\n92\t| Resume harness | [benny_cli.py](../../../benny_cli.py), [benny/persistence/checkpointer.py](../../../benny/persistence/checkpointer.py) | extend |\n93\t| Worker pool / backpressure | [benny/graph/swarm.py](../../../benny/graph/swarm.py), `benny/graph/worker_pool.py` (new) | extend + new |\n94\t| BDD pipeline | `benny/sdlc/requirements.py` (new), `benny/sdlc/bdd.py` (new) | new |\n95\t| TOGAF mapping | `benny/sdlc/togaf.py` (new), template at `manifests/templates/sdlc_pipeline.json` (new) | new |\n96\t| Policy-as-Code | [benny/governance/permission_manifest.py](../../../benny/governance/permission_manifest.py), `benny/governance/policy.py` (new) | extend + new |\n97\t| JSON-LD lineage | [benny/governance/lineage.py](../../../benny/governance/lineage.py), `benny/governance/jsonld.py` (new) | extend + new |\n98\t| Process metrics | `benny/sdlc/sandbox_runner.py` (new), `benny/sdlc/metrics.py` (new) | new |\n99\t| Release gates | [tests/release/test_release_gates.py](../../../tests/release/test_release_gates.py), new `tests/release/test_aos_release_gate.py` | extend + new |\n100\t\n101\t---\n102\t\n103\t## Reading order for a new agent\n104\t\n105\t1. This README (vocabulary + do-not list).\n106\t2. [requirement.md](requirement.md) §1–§3 (scope, actors, contracts).\n107\t3. [project_plan.md](project_plan.md) §3 (phase map) and §5 (risk register).\n108\t4. The Brief (`source_brief.md`) for the *why*.\n109\t5. [acceptance_matrix.md](acceptance_matrix.md) when picking up an open phase.\n110\t"}]},"uuid":"1dfe1ab6-5b6b-4441-adb7-dc72d89a729f","timestamp":"2026-06-23T09:10:20.495Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\runtime\\docs\\requirements\\10\\README.md","content":"# AOS-001 — Agentic Operating System for the SDLC\n\n**Phase:** 10 (succeeds Phase 9 / pypes)\n**Status:** DRAFT — pending OQ resolutions in [requirement.md §13](requirement.md#13-open-questions-must-be-resolved-before-phase-1-merges)\n**Author:** Benny Studio team\n**Last updated:** 2026-04-26\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\n\nPhase 10 closes the loop between Benny's three capability surfaces (documents, code, tabular data) and turns Benny into a **deterministic, portable Agentic Operating System for the entire Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC)**. The driving artefact is the architectural brief *\"Architecting a Deterministic, Portable Agentic Operating System for the Software Development Life Cycle\"* (the **Brief**, attached to this folder as `source_brief.md` once committed).\n\nWhere Phase 9 (pypes) made tabular data first-class